# The root R0 without an entry. The observation of line 17 of the row construction_paths, separated: `cur` is
# redirected from A to B before the call, then the real code of C reads Leaf/B through the reference its parent
# declares and writes the observable into `Log` explicitly: `Log\selected` 2; `Log\before` 1, `Log\after` 1. (With
# `cur` still on A the same body would read 1.) A nested record is written without a space before its parenthesis.
@: Log (int: before 0; int: selected 0; int: after 0)
@: D (
    A(Leaf(int: v 1))
    B(Leaf(int: v 2))
    @: cur A
    C(
        @: saved cur\Leaf
        go:
            Log\selected := saved\v
        end: go
    )
)
Log\before := 1
D\cur := D\B
call(code := D\C\go)
Log\after := 1
